WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:05.629
These days, movie fans are constantly bombarded
with trailers, posters, and new information

00:00:05.629 --> 00:00:08.580
about all kinds of tentpole franchise films.

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:12.900
On the flip side, however, there are a few
upcoming movies that have managed to fly under

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:13.920
the radar.

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:18.340
From sci-fi epics to action-packed thrillers,
here are some of the sequels you might not

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:19.360
know are being made.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.759
After years of speculation that a fourth Matrix
film was in the works, Variety broke the news

00:00:24.759 --> 00:00:30.250
in August 2019 that a new instalment in the
series was indeed on the horizon, and that,

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:34.140
despite previous rumors, it wouldn't be following
a new character after all.

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:38.840
Original stars Keanu Reeves and Carrie Ann
Moss will be returning for The Matrix 4, along

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:41.540
with original writer and director Lana Wachowski.

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:43.500
"Woah."

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:48.580
And while Wachowski may have partnered with
her sister Lilly to make the first three Matrix

00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:52.680
movies, the fourth installment will have only
the one Wachowski at the helm.

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:57.180
In addition to Wachowski, the script for The
Matrix 4 will be co-written by Aleksandar

00:00:57.180 --> 00:01:01.460
Hemon and David Mitchell, and is set to start
production in early 2020.

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:05.240
No plot details have yet been revealed for
the movie, and it isn't yet clear how the

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:09.920
film plans to incorporate Moss' or Reeves'
characters, who were killed in the third film

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:12.580
in the franchise, The Matrix Revolutions.

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:17.540
It is equally unclear whether Laurence Fishburne's
character, Morpheus, will be making an appearance.

00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:21.900
Some sources have speculated that he may be
recast in order to appear as a younger version

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:24.860
of the character, but that remains speculation
for now.

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:30.000
James Cameron has been talking about his Avatar
sequels almost from the moment the first film

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:35.490
exploded onto screens in 2009, smashing box
office records and eventually becoming the

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:37.660
highest-grossing film of all time.

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:43.440
However, despite years of Cameron's repeated
promises of a vast and expansive Avatar franchise,

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:47.869
it was beginning to feel as though a follow-up
was as far off and unreachable as the moon

00:01:47.869 --> 00:01:49.080
of Pandora itself.

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:53.480
But believe it or not, four more Avatars really
do appear to be imminent.

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:57.640
In fact, according to Sigourney Weaver, the
first two have already finished shooting.

00:01:57.640 --> 00:02:03.020
They've even got titles: Avatar: The Way of
Water, Avatar: The Seed Bearer, Avatar: The

00:02:03.021 --> 00:02:06.220
Tulkun Rider, and Avatar: The Quest for Eywa.

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:07.380
What does it all mean?

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:12.400
Well, no one knows, except James Cameron himself
and his eclectic cast, which, in addition

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:17.770
to the original movie's stars, also features
a host of newcomers, including Edie Falco,

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:21.480
Kate Winslet, Michelle Yeoh, Jemaine Clement,
and Vin Diesel.

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:25.060
Everyone else will have to wait until the
end of 2021 to find out.

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:29.840
Avatar: The Way of Water is scheduled for
release on December 17th 2021, with

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:35.820
Avatar: The Seed Bearer arriving on December 22nd
2023, Avatar: The Tulkun Rider following on

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:43.040
December 19th 2025, and Avatar: The Quest
for Eywa concluding the franchise on December 17th 2027.

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:48.740
As the crew of the Nostromo learned the hard
way all the way back in 1979, it's pretty

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:54.040
hard to kill an Alien, and the Alien franchise
seems just as tough as the creature itself.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:59.010
Reflecting on his landmark sci-fi horror film
on its 40th anniversary, director Ridley Scott

00:02:59.010 --> 00:03:04.199
told Variety that a third prequel is indeed
on the way, intended as a follow-up to 2012's

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:07.060
Prometheus and 2017's Alien: Covenant.

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:12.040
Despite generally positive critical reviews,
Covenant underperformed at the box office,

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:14.740
throwing the future of the franchise into
uncertainty.

00:03:14.740 --> 00:03:19.620
But following Disney's acquisition of Fox,
both Scott and Alien's new studio home seem

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:22.460
eager to return to the sinister stars yet
again.

00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:26.859
As for what this third prequel might be about,
only one thing is for sure: it won't follow

00:03:26.859 --> 00:03:28.999
the format of the original Alien.

00:03:28.999 --> 00:03:32.609
Speaking to The Hollywood Reporter, Scott
talked about the need for the franchise to

00:03:32.609 --> 00:03:35.219
continue to evolve in order to succeed.

00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:35.920
He said:

00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:39.260
"You can't keep repeating [the same premise]
because the joke gets boring."

00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:44.780
This next Alien film, tentatively titled Alien:
Awakening, is still in the very early stages,

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:48.120
and none of the cast of Covenant has yet been
asked to return.

00:03:48.129 --> 00:03:52.469
Still, Scott maintains three things: it's
happening, he'll be directing it, and it's

00:03:52.469 --> 00:03:54.120
currently in the script phase.

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:59.459
After the release of the poorly-received Indiana
Jones and the Kingdom of the Crystal Skull,

00:03:59.459 --> 00:04:03.659
no one would've blamed Harrison Ford, Steven
Spielberg, and everyone else at Lucasfilm

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:06.780
if they'd given up on the Indiana Jones franchise
altogether.

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:11.430
But now it appears that Indy will be back
with Indiana Jones 5, which, despite a number

00:04:11.430 --> 00:04:14.880
of push-backs and delays, is still theoretically
happening.

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:19.100
Indiana Jones 5 has gone through a number
of screenwriters already, from Crystal Skull

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:24.730
scribe David Koepp, to Solo's Jonathan Kasdan,
to This Is Us creator Dan Fogelman, and now,

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:26.160
apparently, back to Koepp.

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:30.590
No word has yet been given on what Indiana
Jones 5 will be about, although Harrison Ford

00:04:30.590 --> 00:04:34.980
will be at least 78 when the movie starts
filming, so chances are that the adventure

00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:38.900
will have to be a little less physically rigorous
than previous installments.

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:41.180
"It's not the years, honey.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:43.520
It's the mileage."

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:49.080
Of course, it's possible that even the filmmakers
don't quite know the movie's plot yet.

00:04:49.090 --> 00:04:52.570
Speaking to Den of Geek in September of 2019,
Koepp said:

00:04:52.570 --> 00:04:54.030
"I'm working on it again.

00:04:54.030 --> 00:04:55.030
We're still trying.

00:04:55.030 --> 00:04:56.860
And I think we've got a good idea this time.

00:04:56.860 --> 00:04:57.640
We'll see."

00:04:57.700 --> 00:05:02.520
If Indiana Jones 5 is indeed still hanging
around in the "good idea" stage, it's probably

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:05.570
got a long way to go before it actually hits
theaters.

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:08.460
Still, according to everyone involved, it'll
get there.

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:09.460
Eventually.

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:14.600
Bill may have finally been killed at the end
of 2004's Kill Bill Vol. 2, but that hasn't

00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:19.070
stopped director Quentin Tarantino from expressing
his desire for another sequel to round out

00:05:19.070 --> 00:05:20.060
the trilogy.

00:05:20.060 --> 00:05:24.180
According to Tarantino, the third Kill Bill
would focus on the daughter of Vernita Green,

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:28.290
who is now all grown up and on the hunt for
revenge against the person who killed her

00:05:28.290 --> 00:05:30.300
mother, Uma Thurman's Beatrix.

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:34.680
Tarantino has said that he's had talks with
Thurman about Kill Bill Vol. 3 as recently

00:05:34.690 --> 00:05:37.410
as July of 2019, telling MTV:

00:05:37.410 --> 00:05:41.200
"If any of my movies were going to spring
from my other movies, it would be a third

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:42.040
Kill Bill."

00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:46.800
Of course, a third Kill Bill may throw a wrench
in Tarantino's plans to retire after his tenth

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:51.660
film; his ninth, Once Upon a Time in Hollywood,
hit theaters in the summer of 2019, and his

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:55.400
tenth, an upcoming Star Trek film, is currently
in the works.

00:05:55.400 --> 00:06:00.010
Then again, no one but Tarantino himself is
going to hold him to his self-imposed film

00:06:00.010 --> 00:06:02.220
cap if he chooses to keep going.

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:05.880
Nothing is finalized for a Kill Bill sequel
yet, but it seems as though all that would

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:10.440
be needed for it to materialize is simply
for Tarantino to decide to pull the trigger.

00:06:11.180 --> 00:06:15.060
Although rumor has it that a third Sherlock
Holmes film has always been part of the plan

00:06:15.070 --> 00:06:20.110
over at Warner Bros., Robert Downey Jr. has
spent the past decade leading the Marvel Cinematic

00:06:20.110 --> 00:06:24.260
Universe as the genius billionaire playboy
philanthropist Tony Stark.

00:06:24.260 --> 00:06:28.800
Saving the world every couple years is obviously
a pretty draining gig, and Downey's superhero

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:33.280
commitments kept him from being able to take
up Sherlock's trademark deerstalker and pipe

00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:34.500
for a third time.

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:39.140
But now that Downey has seemingly exited the
MCU for good, he finally has the time to team

00:06:39.140 --> 00:06:43.900
up with Watson, solve one more case, and take
his last bow as the famous detective.

00:06:43.900 --> 00:06:48.640
The third Sherlock Holmes film will be helmed
by Rocketman director Dexter Fletcher, a departure

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:51.880
from the first two films, which were both
directed by Guy Ritchie.

00:06:51.880 --> 00:06:56.880
While Sherlock Holmes 3 was originally scheduled
to release on Christmas Day 2020, it has since

00:06:56.880 --> 00:07:01.280
been pushed back a year, and will now be striding
into theaters in December 2021.

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:07.760
The Hitman's Bodyguard wasn't exactly a critical
success, earning a pretty lousy Rotten Tomatoes score.

00:07:08.020 --> 00:07:14.280
But the movie did pretty well at the box office,
pulling in almost $177 million worldwide against

00:07:14.280 --> 00:07:16.060
a $30 million budget.

00:07:16.060 --> 00:07:20.680
After all, how can an audience possibly say
no to the combined charisma of Ryan Reynolds

00:07:20.680 --> 00:07:22.380
and Samuel L. Jackson?

00:07:22.380 --> 00:07:26.250
Well, fans of the first film will be happy
to know that The Hitman's Bodyguard is getting

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:30.580
a sequel, confusingly titled The Hitman's
Wife's Bodyguard.

00:07:30.580 --> 00:07:35.320
Reynolds and Jackson are both returning, and
Salma Hayek is also coming back at the titular wife.

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:39.720
According to The Hollywood Reporter, the plot
will find Reynolds' bodyguard trying to live

00:07:39.720 --> 00:07:43.740
a peaceful life when he gets mixed up with
Jackson's hitman once more.

00:07:43.740 --> 00:07:48.520
Along with Hayek, the trio will apparently
wreak havoc along the Amalfi Coast in an attempt

00:07:48.520 --> 00:07:51.700
to save Europe from some as-yet-unconfirmed
threat.

00:07:51.700 --> 00:07:57.000
The movie will also star familiar names like
Morgan Freeman, Antonio Banderas, Frank Grillo,

00:07:57.010 --> 00:07:58.260
and Richard E. Grant.

00:07:58.260 --> 00:08:02.440
If you're hoping for a wild time at the movies,
then this is the one for you; insiders are

00:08:02.440 --> 00:08:03.980
describing this film as:

00:08:03.980 --> 00:08:04.600
"The Good.

00:08:04.720 --> 00:08:05.220
The Bad.

00:08:05.320 --> 00:08:06.780
And the Bats--- crazy."

00:08:07.120 --> 00:08:12.000
According to Deadline, RoboCop is indeed returning
to the big screen sometime soon, although

00:08:12.001 --> 00:08:16.100
it seems this new film is going to mess around
with the franchise's continuity.

00:08:16.100 --> 00:08:19.990
The original RoboCop was directed by Paul
Verhoeven, and it made quite a killing when

00:08:19.990 --> 00:08:22.230
it was released in 1987.

00:08:22.230 --> 00:08:27.000
After two sequels starring original actor
Peter Weller, the franchise was rebooted in

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:30.440
2014, with actor Joel Kinnaman and director
Jose Padilha.

00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:34.780
The remake wasn't nearly as popular as the
first film, and sadly for Mr. Kinnaman, it

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:38.280
looks like the new movie is going to ignore
the recent remake altogether.

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:42.479
The latest entry in the franchise will be
called RoboCop Returns, and is written by

00:08:42.480 --> 00:08:46.060
Ed Neumeier and Michael Miner, the guys who
penned the first film.

00:08:46.060 --> 00:08:50.480
In fact, RoboCop Returns was apparently written
right after the original was released.

00:08:50.490 --> 00:08:55.529
Sadly, the script never got made into a movie,
but now MGM is giving it another go, with

00:08:55.529 --> 00:08:59.360
the help of some rewrites by Terminator: Dark
Fate writer Justin Rhodes.

00:08:59.360 --> 00:09:03.120
Sadly, Peter Weller won't be returning to
reprise his robo-role.

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:05.740
As for the plot synopsis, Deadline writes:

00:09:05.750 --> 00:09:10.370
"Anarchy reigns and the fate of Detroit hangs
in the balance as RoboCop makes his triumphant

00:09:10.370 --> 00:09:12.559
return to fight crime and corruption."

00:09:12.560 --> 00:09:17.080
Though District 9's Neill Blomkamp was initially
attached to direct, he announced in August

00:09:17.080 --> 00:09:21.200
2019 that scheduling conflicts had forced
him to depart the project.

00:09:21.209 --> 00:09:26.089
In November 2019, Orion Pictures announced
that Little Monsters director Abe Forsythe

00:09:26.089 --> 00:09:30.220
had taken up the helm of RoboCop Returns,
and would also be giving the screenplay a

00:09:30.220 --> 00:09:31.020
fresh rewrite.

00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:32.820
"Your move, creep."

00:09:34.260 --> 00:09:38.400
What do you get when you cross a horde of
hungry zombies with a very fast train?

00:09:38.400 --> 00:09:42.780
A critically acclaimed blockbuster that desperately
needs a sequel, apparently.

00:09:42.780 --> 00:09:48.500
Released in 2016, Train to Busan earned $85
million in its homeland of South Korea, and

00:09:48.509 --> 00:09:50.460
wowed critics across the globe.

00:09:50.460 --> 00:09:54.610
The plot follows a selfish businessman who's
taking his daughter on a train ride to the

00:09:54.610 --> 00:09:58.800
city of Busan, when zombies suddenly start
popping up all over the place.

00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:03.420
At first, the protagonist is only concerned
with protecting himself and his kid, but as

00:10:03.420 --> 00:10:07.749
things get bloodier and bloodier, he starts
helping the other passengers escape the oncoming

00:10:07.749 --> 00:10:08.420
horde.

00:10:08.420 --> 00:10:13.120
Now, it seems writer-director Yeon Sang-ho
is working on part two, supposedly titled

00:10:13.120 --> 00:10:13.700
Bando.

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:17.660
The English title is being reported to be
"Peninsula," which seems to imply that the

00:10:17.660 --> 00:10:19.920
zombie virus has spread across Korea.

00:10:19.920 --> 00:10:24.520
Shooting began in the summer of 2019, with
a new cast stepping in front of the camera.

00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:29.079
It's evidently a good time to be in the zombie
train business, as New Line is currently working

00:10:29.080 --> 00:10:31.200
on an American remake of the first film.

00:10:31.200 --> 00:10:35.100
Of course, if you're new to the whole Train
to Busan phenomenon, you can prepare for both

00:10:35.100 --> 00:10:39.700
the sequel and the reboot by checking out
the 2016 thriller in all its bloody glory

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:40.760
over on Netflix.

00:10:41.760 --> 00:10:46.290
Sylvester Stallone and The Expendables 4 have
been engaging in a will-they-won't-they dance

00:10:46.290 --> 00:10:51.100
for a few years now, but the latest signs
seem to point definitively to "they will".

00:10:51.100 --> 00:10:55.639
Taking to his own Instagram account, Stallone
announced in July 2019 that the sequel was

00:10:55.639 --> 00:10:59.720
back on, with a photo of the star in his Expendables
gear and the caption:

00:10:59.720 --> 00:11:02.690
"All of those July 4th fireworks got my mind
going!

00:11:02.690 --> 00:11:04.879
I am starting to cook up the next adventure!"

00:11:04.880 --> 00:11:09.060
Stallone directed, co-wrote, and starred in
the original Expendables, which came out in

00:11:09.060 --> 00:11:09.980
2010.

00:11:10.200 --> 00:11:14.740
He also helped write the existing two sequels,
although for those, he handed off directorial

00:11:14.750 --> 00:11:18.079
duties to Simon West for 2 and Patrick Hughes
for 3.

00:11:18.079 --> 00:11:23.060
He walked away from The Expendables 4 back
in 2017, but his exit appears to have been

00:11:23.060 --> 00:11:24.160
only temporary.

00:11:24.160 --> 00:11:28.980
In addition to Stallone, the Expendables franchise
has been a veritable Who's Who of current

00:11:28.980 --> 00:11:33.639
and former action superstars, but only Jason
Statham and Arnold Schwarzenegger have been

00:11:33.640 --> 00:11:36.560
confirmed as joining Stallone in The Expendables
4.

00:11:39.360 --> 00:11:40.760
"I'm back."

00:11:40.960 --> 00:11:44.900
If and when Stallone does finalize the fourth
installment in the series, though, you can

00:11:44.910 --> 00:11:49.250
expect the cast list to grow exponentially,
with an even more impressive collection of

00:11:49.250 --> 00:11:51.260
stars than the previous three films.

00:11:52.060 --> 00:11:56.620
After the runaway success of The Hunger Games
series of books and films, it seemed likely

00:11:56.620 --> 00:12:01.660
that audiences would one day return to the
dystopian world of Panem, one way or another.

00:12:01.660 --> 00:12:06.740
And sure enough, in June 2019, publisher Scholastic
announced that it would be releasing another

00:12:06.740 --> 00:12:10.020
novel by Suzanne Collins set in the Hunger
Games world.

00:12:10.020 --> 00:12:14.680
This book would be a prequel, set 64 years
before the events of the original story, and

00:12:14.680 --> 00:12:16.740
would focus on the tenth Hunger Games.

00:12:16.740 --> 00:12:22.260
In October 2019, the book's title was revealed:
The Ballad of Songbirds and Snakes.

00:12:22.260 --> 00:12:26.140
Along with the announcement of the novel came
the confirmation that Collins' prequel will

00:12:26.149 --> 00:12:28.189
also receive the movie treatment.

00:12:28.189 --> 00:12:32.311
Lionsgate chairman Joe Drake, whose studio
adapted the Hunger Games films, said of the

00:12:32.311 --> 00:12:33.311
book announcement:

00:12:33.311 --> 00:12:37.730
"As the proud home of the Hunger Games movies,
we can hardly wait for Suzanne's next book

00:12:37.730 --> 00:12:38.840
to be published.

00:12:38.840 --> 00:12:42.999
We've been communicating with her during the
writing process and we look forward to continuing

00:12:42.999 --> 00:12:45.139
to work closely with her on the movie."

00:12:45.139 --> 00:12:50.279
The Ballad of Songbirds and Snakes is scheduled
to hit bookshelves on May 19th 2020, and from

00:12:50.280 --> 00:12:54.220
the sounds of things, more news about the
film adaptation will be right on its heels.

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:59.200
Directed by the one and only John Carpenter,
Big Trouble in Little China is one of the

00:12:59.200 --> 00:13:01.460
wackiest action movies ever made.

00:13:01.460 --> 00:13:06.580
This 1986 fantasy-adventure follows trucker
Jack Burton as he attempts to save a kidnapped

00:13:06.580 --> 00:13:10.880
woman from the dark and magical underbelly
of San Francisco's Chinatown.

00:13:10.880 --> 00:13:15.699
With its Mortal Kombat-style warriors and
magical sword fights, Big Trouble in Little

00:13:15.699 --> 00:13:20.639
China has become a beloved classic, so naturally
people were a bit worried when a remake with

00:13:20.639 --> 00:13:23.399
Dwayne Johnson was announced in 2015.

00:13:23.399 --> 00:13:26.939
There hasn't been a lot of new info since
then, but it's now clear that the new Big

00:13:26.939 --> 00:13:29.300
Trouble will actually be a sequel.

00:13:29.300 --> 00:13:32.260
Speaking to Collider, producer Hiram Garcia
admitted:

00:13:32.440 --> 00:13:37.300
"You can't remake a classic like [Big Trouble],
so what we're planning to do is continue the story.

00:13:37.540 --> 00:13:41.020
We're going to continue the universe of Big
Trouble in Little China."

00:13:41.029 --> 00:13:45.140
As Garcia went on to explain, the events of
the first film will still exist in the new

00:13:45.140 --> 00:13:46.649
Dwayne Johnson movie.

00:13:46.649 --> 00:13:50.860
On top of that, the Rock will be playing a
brand new character, rather than Jack Burton.

00:13:51.060 --> 00:13:55.140
So it seems they're taking a page from the
Jurassic World playbook, by crafting a movie

00:13:55.149 --> 00:13:59.810
that exists in a pre-established timeline,
but also serves as a kind of reboot for a

00:13:59.810 --> 00:14:01.050
new generation.

00:14:01.050 --> 00:14:06.179
Unfortunately, Kurt Russell has told USA Today
that he probably won't be in the sequel, so

00:14:06.180 --> 00:14:09.660
Burton himself sadly won't be back in action
for this one.

00:14:10.320 --> 00:14:14.160
Nobody messes with the Jesus...except for
John Turturro, that is.

00:14:14.160 --> 00:14:18.340
After all, Turturro played the purple-clad
Jesus in The Big Lebowski, and even though

00:14:18.350 --> 00:14:23.060
he's only onscreen for two scenes, the pervy
bowler apparently made enough of an impression

00:14:23.060 --> 00:14:25.060
to warrant his own spin-off movie.

00:14:25.060 --> 00:14:30.079
Once called Going Places, it's now known as
The Jesus Rolls, and it has absolutely nothing

00:14:30.079 --> 00:14:31.399
to do with the Dude.

00:14:31.399 --> 00:14:37.300
"Yeah, well, that's just, you know, like,
your opinion, man."

00:14:37.300 --> 00:14:42.000
The plot follows Jesus, who's just been released
from jail after he was framed for a crime

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:43.220
he didn't commit.

00:14:43.220 --> 00:14:47.500
Now a free man, he teams up with two friends
and goes on a wild road trip.

00:14:47.500 --> 00:14:50.780
According to the film's official plot synopsis,
the movie is:

00:14:50.790 --> 00:14:56.570
"A film about a trio of misfits whose irreverent,
sexually charged dynamic evolves into a surprising

00:14:56.570 --> 00:15:01.850
love story as their spontaneous and flippant
attitude towards the past or future backfires

00:15:01.850 --> 00:15:05.829
time and again, even as they inadvertently
perform good deeds."

00:15:05.829 --> 00:15:11.040
In September 2019, a trailer for The Jesus
Rolls appeared, albeit one dubbed in Italian

00:15:11.040 --> 00:15:13.040
to promote the film's release in Italy.

00:15:13.040 --> 00:15:17.579
As for the dynamic directing duo, the Coens
aren't involved with this spinoff sequel,

00:15:17.580 --> 00:15:20.500
but they're still totally cool with Turturro
making a part two.

00:15:20.980 --> 00:15:25.760
Almost two decades after the first Space Jam
mashed up live action comedy, Looney Tunes

00:15:25.769 --> 00:15:30.720
animation, and professional basketball, Warner
Brothers announced in early 2014 that they'd

00:15:30.720 --> 00:15:33.569
be making a follow up to the 1996 film.

00:15:33.569 --> 00:15:38.410
The original Space Jam starred NBA superstar
Michael Jordan, and featured appearances from

00:15:38.410 --> 00:15:41.980
a number of other NBA players alongside its
animated cast.

00:15:41.980 --> 00:15:47.600
The sequel will star NBA MVP LeBron James,
in addition to Don Cheadle, fresh off his

00:15:47.600 --> 00:15:51.160
almost decade-long stint in the Marvel Cinematic
Universe.

00:15:51.160 --> 00:15:55.079
With a production team that includes Black
Panther's Ryan Coogler and The Fast and the

00:15:55.079 --> 00:16:00.069
Furious series' Justin Lin, Space Jam 2 will
be helmed by director Malcolm D. Lee.

00:16:00.069 --> 00:16:04.180
Lee wasn't the first director attached to
the film, though; he stepped in for Terence

00:16:04.180 --> 00:16:09.499
Nance, who departed the production on good
terms in July 2019, citing creative differences.

00:16:09.499 --> 00:16:15.069
The film is set to hit theaters on July 16th
2021, almost a full quarter of a century after

00:16:15.069 --> 00:16:17.170
the first film premiered.

00:16:17.170 --> 00:16:19.329
